{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Many days.</b> The tradition of our Rabbis, of blessed memory: ״ימים רבים״ — ״ימים״, two; ״רבים״, three. And so they said: ״ימים״ — two; one might think ״ימים הרבה״ — many; Rabbi Akiva said: Whatever can be heard as many and can be heard as few — if you take it as many you have not grasped it; if you take it as few you have grasped it. Rabbi Nehemiah said: Now what does the verse come to do — to open or to close? Surely it comes not to close but to open. For if you say ״ימים״ means ten, it could be a hundred; it could be two hundred; it could be a thousand; it could be ten thousand; but when you say ״ימים״ means two, you have opened. Rabbi Muna said: ״ימים״ — two; one might think ״ימים הרבה״ — many; but if they were many, has it not already been said ״רבים״? Thus the verse speaks only of few days. How many? You must say two. ״רבים״ — three; one might think ״רבים״ means ten. It says ״ימים״ and it says ״רבים״: just as ״ימים״ is a small number, ״ימים״ being two, so ״רבים״ is a small number, ״רבים״ being three. One might think two and three, making five — but was it said ״ימים ורבים״? Surely it was not said so but ״ימים רבים״. How so? These ״רבים״ must be more than the two, and how many are they? You must say three." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> ״ימים רבים״ — but surely the days of menstruation are seven; why does it call them ״ימים רבים״? And likewise (1 Kings 18:1): ״ויהי ימים רבים ודבר ה׳ היה אל אליהו בשנה השלישית לאמר לך הראה אל אחאב ואתנה מטר וגו׳״ — and those were not three full years but one month of the first year and the entire second year and one month of the third; rather, because they were days of trouble they were called ״ימים רבים״. Similar to it (Joshua 11:18): ״ימים רבים עשה יהושע את כל המלכים האלה מלחמה.״ Similar to it (2 Chronicles 15:3): ״והימים רבים לישראל ללא אלהי אמת וללא כהן מורה וללא תורה״ — rather, because they served idolatry it called them ״רבים״. So too here: a woman separates from her husband, and these are days of distress; therefore it called them ״ימים רבים״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:39.843424408Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}